        "text_37BRNF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Product Description</p>",
            "class": "sn-uppercase"
          }
        },
        "text_dLtfq9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>What is the VTrack, and who is it for?</h2><p>The VTrack Overhead Golf Launch Monitor is developed by Laon People Co., Ltd. — an AI-focused golf technology company dedicated to advancing what's possible in photometric tracking. It's a ceiling-mounted, dual-camera launch monitor built for golfers who want a permanent, clean simulator setup with studio-grade data, without the compromises that come with floor-based systems or the price tag of the highest-end commercial units.</p><p>VTrack uses two stereoscopic high-speed cameras — capturing up to 1,800 frames per second — to measure the ball and club through impact from above. Because the system is optical and overhead, there's nothing in your hitting area. The floor stays clear. The swing path is unobstructed. And because VTrack is ceiling-mounted in front of the hitting zone, it naturally supports both left- and right-handed golfers without any repositioning.</p><p>The hitting zone is a generous 31\" × 24\", giving players more flexibility in ball position and stance than tighter alternatives. Shot feedback arrives in approximately 200–250 milliseconds, keeping simulator play feeling connected and responsive. And because VTrack captures slow-motion impact video automatically, you can see exactly what happened at contact — not just what the numbers say.</p><p>VTrack requires a minimum ceiling height of 106\" for proper installation and performance. If your space meets that threshold, it's one of the most compelling overhead launch monitors available for home simulators and private studios at this price point.</p>",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
